  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Description and Construction
    
    A ceremonial vessel of shadow-steel and volcanic glass, roughly the size of a penguin's closed flipper, designed to hold a flame-heart crystal at its core. Forged by Glow-Trader Vaulius-phantasm~ in the Nightshelf settlement of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ during the Clever Ice Age to seal the founding authority of The Cell, the owl-sworn Nightshelf faction. The shadow-steel frame bears the binding-marks of the Pactum∴silenti — authentication-glyphs that glow faintly when the lantern burns. Vaulius-phantasm~ housed the fire-core in corrupted volcanic glass — a deliberate design in which the corruption's bioluminescent chemistry functions as a thermal valve, siphoning excess heat from the core and preventing it from reaching exhaustion.
    
    The ☽'ofund' Guild, a diminished Nightshelf trade faction, claims prior forging. The Cell does not dignify the claim with denial.
    
    ## Damage Record
    
    The glass carries three distinct fracture patterns — hairline cracks from the factional conflict known as Schism (frost-wailed), a long jagged scar from The Bra∴conflictu, and a concentric spiderweb from The Mbra∴silentiu — yet the cracks have never propagated into failure. Keeper-Registrar ☽'noctmuluevus 'born's deep-archive report classifies the damage as Incursion-related and irreversible, consistent with a pattern observed across several Nightshelf relics.
    
    ## Anomalous Properties
    
    The flame has never been extinguished, though hands have tried. It has burned three colors: gold, then red, now a blue so dark it resembles absence. Carriers report its weight increases with each lie told in its presence. More troubling: deep-archive registrars have documented the weight growing between measurements when no lies were told at all. Measurements of the Luminary's radiant output exceed that of a fresh Class III fire-core — an impossibility for a core that has been burning since before living memory.
    
    The flame requires no oil. Its keeper refills it regardless.
    
    ## Current Status and Use
    
    The Luminary rests in ☽'slew Ravium~, a Nightshelf tunnel settlement, classified by The Cell as marginal inventory — a designation that sits uneasily beside the care devoted to tending it. The merchant collective Collective☽ Of Led∴merch presses the lantern's flame into fire-core wax as their commercial seal, branding goods with an unextinguished fire they do not maintain.
    
    The Cell keeps it burning. The summary is correct about why: letting the flame die would concede that the Pactum∴silenti — the accord the lantern was forged to authenticate — is void. What the flame costs to sustain is not recorded.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
